   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The height of a ball above the ground, in meters, is \\( y(t) = 3 t^{2} + 5 t + 19 \\) for time t in seconds. At what rate is the height of the ball changing at the instant t = 5 seconds?",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 35
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "An average rate is available over any interval, so take the short interval from t = 5 to t = 5 + h. The average rate over it is \\( \\frac{y(5 + h) - y(5)}{h} \\).",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change over a short interval"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Expanding and dividing by h leaves \\( \\frac{y(5 + h) - y(5)}{h} = 3 h + 35 \\), which still depends on the length h of the interval.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               "h"
            ],
            35
         ],
         "rule_named": "difference quotient simplified"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The rate at the instant is what these averages approach as h approaches 0: \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{y(5 + h) - y(5)}{h} = 35 \\). This limit is the derivative \\( y'(5) \\).",
         "mathjson": 35,
         "rule_named": "limit of the difference quotient"
      }
   ],
